00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:20.819
your credit score to carry over some debt on credit cards month to month, or just pay it off completely?"

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:27.119
It is better to pay off your credit card balances in full if you have the money to do so. You don't want to necessarily like deplete

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:29.518
your cash reserves because then if an emergency comes up

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:34.349
You'll have nothing to tap into - and this is a four-minute show so most of this is probably cut, but for the record:

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:39.779
there is a part of your credit score that is determined by how much of your available credit

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:43.530
you are using. So obviously there's the argument to be made that when you pay off a

00:00:43.719 --> 00:00:50.038
credit card in full you are reducing the amount of "credit utilization", as they call it, which will help your score.

00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:54.239
But it is much worse for your score to miss a payment than to have a higher utilization.

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:57.058
But if I use all of my credit, then that's not helping my credit score.

00:00:57.059 --> 00:01:01.198
No, that's a bad thing. - That's a bad thing. So long story short: better to pay it off if you can,

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:05.519
but if you can't pay it all off the most important part is making that payment on time.

